  "explanation": "The question asks when the Swedish Evangelical Lutheran Church was built. Multiple distinct referents exist for the name 'Swedish Evangelical Lutheran Church' in the provided sources:\n\n1. **Swedish Evangelical Lutheran Church (Ham Lake, Minnesota)**: Document D1S3 states that the church was built in 1872. Document D2S2 confirms this with the chronology stating the first rendition of the church was built in 1872.\n\n2. **Swedish Evangelical Lutheran Church (Millville, Minnesota)**: Document D4S2 and D6S1 both state that the church was built in 1874.\n\n3. **Swedish Evangelical Lutheran Church (Swedesburg, Iowa)**: Document D7S3 and D8S2 indicate that the current church was built in 1928. Additionally, D3S4 mentions a church in the same general area (Walnut Grove, Minnesota) was erected in 1890 and dismantled in 1925.\n\nEach of these is a separate instance of the church with its own construction date. Therefore, all four dates—1872, 1874, 1890, and 1928—are valid answers corresponding to different locations and instances of the church."
}

